k+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjAnd when he was full forty years old, it came into his heart to visit his brethren the children of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqAnd seeing one of them suffer wrong, he defended him, and avenged him that was oppressed, and smote the Egyptian:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxfor he supposed his brethren would have understood how that God by his hand would deliver them: but they understood not.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¡And the next day he shewed himself unto them as they strove, and would have set them at one again, saying, Sirs, ye are brethren; why do ye wrong one to another?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgBut he that did his neighbour wrong thrust him away, saying, Who made thee a ruler and a judge over us?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ:Wilt thou kill me, as thou diddest the Egyptian yesterday?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbThen fled Moses at this saying, and was a stranger in the land of Madian, where he begat two sons.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse"¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹And when forty years were expired, there appeared to him in the wilderness of mount Sina an angel of the Lord in a flame of fire in a bush.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsWhen Moses saw it, he wondered at the sight: and as he drew near to behold it, the voice of the Lord came unto him,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsaying, I am the God of thy fathers, the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob. Then Moses trembled, and durst not behold.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmThen said the Lord to him, Put off thy shoes from thy feet: for the place where thou standest is holy ground.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙµI have seen, I have seen the affliction of my people which is in Egypt, and I have heard their groaning, and am come down to deliver them. And now come, I will send thee into Egypt.¦layout ªlast_verse"…¤book+§chapter«first_verse#ªlast_verse%¦verses“„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¸This Moses whom they refused, saying, Who made thee a ruler and a judge? the same did God send to be a ruler and a deliverer by the hand of the angel which appeared to him in the bush.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒHe brought them out, after that he had shewed wonders and signs in the land of Egypt, and in the Red sea, and in the wilderness forty years.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¢This is that Moses, which said unto the children of Israel, A prophet shall the Lord your God raise up unto you of your brethren, like unto me; him shall ye hear.¦layout ªlast_verse%…¤book+§chapter«first_verse&ªlast_verse+¦verses–„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ°This is he, that was in the church in the wilderness with the angel which spake to him in the mount Sina, and with our fathers: who received the lively oracles to give unto us:¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoto whom our fathers would not obey, but thrust him from them, and in their hearts turned back again into Egypt,¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”saying unto Aaron, Make us gods to go before us: for as for this Moses, which brought us out of the land of Egypt, we wot not what is become of him.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvAnd they made a calf in those days, and offered sacrifice unto the idol, and rejoiced in the works of their own hands.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤textÙnThen God turned, and gave them up to worship the host of heaven; as it is written in the book of the prophets,¦layout ‚¤textÙGO ye house of Israel, have ye offered to me slain beasts and sacrifices¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ.By the space of forty years in the wilderness?¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ)Yea, ye took up the tabernacle of Moloch,¦layout ‚¤textÙ!And the star of your god Remphan,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ&Figures which ye made to worship them:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ)And I will carry you away beyond Babylon.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse+…¤book+§chapter«first_verse,ªlast_verse2¦verses—„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨Our fathers had the tabernacle of witness in the wilderness, as he had appointed, speaking unto Moses, that he should make it according to the fashion that he had seen.¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¬Which also our fathers that came after brought in with Jesus into the possession of the Gentiles, whom God drave out before the face of our fathers, unto the days of David;¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSwho found favour before God, and desired to find a tabernacle for the God of Jacob.¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤text¿But Solomon built him an house.¦layout ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTHowbeit the most High dwelleth not in temples made with hands; as saith the prophet,¦layout ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤text´Heaven is my throne,¦layout ‚¤textºAnd earth is my footstool:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ,What house will ye build me? saith the Lord:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ Or what is the place of my rest?¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse1„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ'Hath not my hand made all these things?¦layout ªlast_verse2…¤book+§chapter«first_verse3ªlast_verse5¦verses“„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvYe stiffnecked and uncircumcised in heart and ears, ye do always resist the Holy Ghost: as your fathers did, so do ye.¦layout ªlast_verse3„¥verse4¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹Which of the prophets have not your fathers persecuted? and they have slain them which shewed before of the coming of the Just One; of whom ye have been now the betrayers and murderers:¦layout ªlast_verse4„¥verse5¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMwho have received the law by the disposition of angels, and have not kept it.¦layout ªlast_verse5…¤book+§chapter«first_verse6ªlast_verse8¦verses“„¥verse6¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙcWhen they heard these things, they were cut to the heart, and they gnashed on him with their teeth.¦layout ªlast_verse6„¥verse7¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBut he, being full of the Holy Ghost, looked up stedfastly into heaven, and saw the glory of God, and Jesus standing on the right hand of God,¦layout ªlast_verse7„¥verse8¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaand said, Behold, I see the heavens opened, and the Son of man standing on the right hand of God.¦layout ªlast_verse8…¤book+§chapter«first_verse9ªlast_verse<¦verses”„¥verse9¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`Then they cried out with a loud voice, and stopped their ears, and ran upon him with one accord,¦layout ªlast_verse9„¥verse:¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒand cast him out of the city, and stoned him: and the witnesses laid down their clothes at a young man's feet, whose name was Saul.¦layout ªlast_verse:„¥verse;¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUAnd they stoned Stephen, calling upon God, and saying, Lord Jesus, receive my spirit.¦layout ªlast_verse;„¥verse<¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„And he kneeled down, and cried with a loud voice, Lord, lay not this sin to their charge. And when he had said this, he fell asleep.¦layout ªlast_verse<